{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1442717-supporter-merit-in-w20","id":1442717,"title":"Supporter Merit in W20","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-04-05T06:48:48-07:00","id":1442717,"title":"Supporter Merit in W20","content":"So, when it says you have a -2 difficulty on Social rolls, what do they mean exactly? Because that can't mean what I think it means for a 2 point merit. Either my friend's copy of the book is outdated or Social rolls is a lot more narrowly defined.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/723-talam","name":"Talam","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"182"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-05T14:01:32-07:00","id":1442766,"title":"","content":"There hasn't been an official clarification on this one, but pretty much everyone I know agrees that the wording in the book is far too broadly stated.<br /> <br /> The most common narrowing I have seen is just to reference back to the beginning of the Merit: you get a -2 diff on Social rolls to inspire people.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":617,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","user":"Heavy Arms","date":". 04-05-2021, 05:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-07T07:24:56-07:00","id":1442967,"title":"","content":"A sensible alteration, since that would follow in theme.<br /> <br /> Mind you, my group apparently is sticking with it being a generic -2 after I did my do-diligence by bringing it up with them, so I guess I have one overly good merit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/723-talam","name":"Talam","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"182"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-07T09:14:34-07:00","id":1442978,"title":"","content":"There were plenty of 1 dot Merits in older editions (some of the game lines just turned this into a generic Merit) that gave you a flat -2 difficulty break to any use of a given Ability. A lot of people are used to being able to throw that down as a bonus relatively cheaply. By itself it's not that powerful (there's a common Rank 1 Gift that provides the same bonus) depending on how your group handles social stuff. It's mostly a problem when you get into stacking bonuses from multiple sources and you're suddenly tossing around a dozen dice at -4 difficulty and social obstacles might as well not be bothered with.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-07T16:08:09-07:00","id":1443045,"title":"","content":"Persuasion, I have that gift too. It only gives a -1, but a -3 to difficulty is pretty sweet if you make the roll and your social roll is super effective, so yea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"use